Begin reproducible computational work from zero (@rc-reading: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @reproducible-computation, #source "sources/Scientific-Python-Sundnes.lingua#r_1V7KWH76GSD7XMA9TQVSTEQSWB", #source "sources/Research-Software-Engineering.lingua#r_07D4PDD4HGKNK3PW4M90YSV2QY", #source "sources/Scientific-Computing-Practices.lingua#r_5J8HXCQDNJH59EZC1PRJTQK38B", #reproducible-computation "foundations/Question-and-claim.lingua#r_2G13323XWBD8ZQD7S8FVE13AT0") { r_7PQM3TCWSZAA50H4HQ0YF55ZJY
**Read:** [Introduction to Scientific Programming with Python — Sundnes](sources/Scientific-Python-Sundnes.lingua#r_1V7KWH76GSD7XMA9TQVSTEQSWB), the whole book and exercises; [Research Software Engineering with Python — Irving and colleagues](sources/Research-Software-Engineering.lingua#r_07D4PDD4HGKNK3PW4M90YSV2QY), the whole book after the initial language preparation; [Good enough practices in scientific computing — Wilson and colleagues](sources/Scientific-Computing-Practices.lingua#r_5J8HXCQDNJH59EZC1PRJTQK38B), the complete paper as an initial map.

Start with an ordinary calculation whose inputs and meaning can be explained. No earlier programming course is assumed. Use [Quantitative and technical literacy](../quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2) where arithmetic, units, functions, or graphs need preparation. The early Records introduce the files, language, and command-line ideas actually used; the advanced work later demands numerical and scholarly depth.

Read [Introduction to Scientific Programming with Python — Sundnes](sources/Scientific-Python-Sundnes.lingua#r_1V7KWH76GSD7XMA9TQVSTEQSWB) completely, doing the exercises. Its first five chapters support the first saved calculation; later chapters develop arrays, plotting, dictionaries, classes, and object-oriented organization. Complete [The Unix Shell — Software Carpentry](sources/Unix-Shell.lingua#r_5YJ6K2A69H1D45AADES3QR94AX) in parallel once the file/process Records make its commands intelligible. The official Python tutorial is a companion after these introductions, since it assumes some programming knowledge.

When loops, functions, and file reading are usable, undertake the whole [Research Software Engineering with Python — Irving and colleagues](sources/Research-Software-Engineering.lingua#r_07D4PDD4HGKNK3PW4M90YSV2QY) and its substantial project in sequence. Read [Pro Git — Chacon and Straub](sources/Pro-Git.lingua#r_7NQ43JGJ863RMR0HDHA7GMRD9G) chapters 1–3 and 5, later 7 and 10, and complete [The Good Research Code Handbook — Mineault and community](sources/Good-Research-Code.lingua#r_771ZMSHAY1TCSTFCHPT9KZRA66) with its numerical-testing extension. These are substantial readings with exercises, not a few linked definitions. Reuse the original small analysis throughout so each new practice has a concrete purpose.

Then deepen environments/workflows through primary manuals, floating point through [What Every Computer Scientist Should Know About Floating-Point Arithmetic — Goldberg](sources/Floating-Point-Goldberg.lingua#r_4FHXH9WWX5Q535CD32ESSVSEHH), and stochastic study through the shared metrology material and the complete JCGM guide. Select a substantive environment and workflow method for practical reconstruction and compare alternatives; using every tool in one project is unnecessary.

The sustained projects, published-result reproduction, and independent investigation develop practical and academic depth. [What completing reproducible computational work means](research/Completion.lingua#r_7VYT5A5V6ZS9K32WJQK6786NZT) describes the learning evidence expected at the end. Begin easily, return to missing preparation at the point of use, and keep the later scientific demands intact.

**Continue:** [Begin with a question and a result someone can check](foundations/Question-and-claim.lingua#r_2G13323XWBD8ZQD7S8FVE13AT0).

**Return:** [Reproducible computational work](Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ).
